[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112612,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seromucinous hamartoma (SH) is a benign proliferation of small eosinophilic glands arising in the sinonasal tract.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112613,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112614,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112615,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> microglandular adenosis of the nose; glandular hamartoma; serous hamartoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112616,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112617,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SH arises in the nasal cavity and paranasal sinuses, typically in the posterior nasal septum and nasopharynx {29594917}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112618,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common symptoms are nasal obstruction, purulent rhinorrhoea, and epistaxis {29380040; 30407294}. Endoscopically, a papillomatous lesion is usually seen, sometimes with concurrent inflammatory nasal polyps {21618016}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>SH is well defined and homogeneous on both CT and MRI {30765377}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112619,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SH is rare. It has an equal sex distribution, with a wide age range (11&ndash;86&nbsp;years) at presentation {19207945; 20922408; 21618016; 24817677}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112620,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112621,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>One case harboured an <em>EGFR</em>::<em>ZNF267</em> gene fusion, and another case displayed monoclonality by AR X-chromosome inactivation assay, supporting the hypothesis of a neoplastic process {31698004}. Mitochondrial DNA revealed a slightly increased mutation rate mainly in heteroplasmy, consistent with a benign neoplasm {20922408}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112622,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SH presents as a polypoid mass, ranging from 4&nbsp;to 60&nbsp;mm {19207945}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112623,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SH is a polypoid lesion lined by respiratory ciliated epithelium, with many small eosinophilic glands in the stroma, resembling microglandular adenosis of the breast {19207945; 20922408; 21618016; 24817677}. SH displays a lobular or horizontal distribution, with no infiltrative growth. Tubules are small and uniform, and they may contain an amorphous eosinophilic material; they are lined by epithelial cuboidal cells with small nuclei, without mitoses. Myoepithelial/basal cells are absent, or only focally present {22392408}, but basal lamina around tubules is discernible. The tubules may be seen between native bony elements, but no true destructive infiltration is seen. No complex architectural patterns have been identified, such as exophytic growth, papillary architecture, or gland fusion.</p>\r\n<p>The small glands of SH are sometimes combined with cystic structures lined by respiratory epithelium and p63-positive basal cells, more characteristic of respiratory epithelial adenomatoid hamartoma. Mixed forms exist as well.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112624,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112625,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112626,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a monotonous proliferation of small tubules without atypia; absent/rare myoepithelial/basal cells; discernible basal lamina; no infiltrative pattern; no papillary architecture or gland fusion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112627,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112628,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrences are rare after complete excision {19207945}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:36:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
